### Changes made to the upstream

The LGPL requires modified files to be marked as changed and dated. The list below was produced by
diffing this tree against the official source archive of the same tag
(`MsdialWorkbench-MSDIAL-v5.5.260817.tar.gz` from the upstream repository, 2026-09-15). **These six
files are the whole of it** — nothing was added to the upstream tree and nothing was removed from
it.

| File | What changed |
| --- | --- |
| `src/MSDIAL5/MsdialCore/MsdialCore.csproj` | a build switch, `UseOpenRawData`. When it is set, the closed `RawDataHandler` package references are dropped and the port's own open raw-data project is referenced instead, and `Microsoft.Data.Sqlite` replaces `System.Data.SQLite.Core`, which has no native library for `osx-arm64` |
| `src/MSDIAL5/MsdialCore/DataObj/EadLipidSqliteDatabase.cs` | the SQLite types are aliased to `Microsoft.Data.Sqlite` behind an `OPENDIAL_SQLITE` conditional; the ADO.NET surface used here is identical, so the body is unchanged |
| `src/Common/CommonStandard/MessagePack/LargeListMessagePack.cs` | a short read fed the unsafe LZ4 decoder and crashed the process when a processed `.mdproject` was opened; the read is now checked (2026-09-13) |
| `tests/MSDIAL5/MsdialCoreTestApp/Program.cs` | seven lines that force the invariant culture at start-up. MS-DIAL parses numbers with the current culture in method files, MSP libraries and mzML values, so on a decimal-comma locale it silently produced zero peaks |
| `tests/MSDIAL5/MsdialCoreTestApp/Parser/AnalysisFilesParser.cs` | one line: a path built by concatenation became `Path.Combine`, which is what makes it work off Windows |
| `tests/MSDIAL5/MsdialCoreTestApp/Process/CommonProcess.cs` | SCIEX IDA: the precursor is taken per scan rather than from the dependent experiment's placeholder, which was assigning every product spectrum the same mass (2026-09-07) |

Every change carries an `OpenDIAL:` comment at the point of the edit, so they can be found in the
tree as well as read here.

## What is not here

- **SCIEX Clearcore2** — the assemblies that let the SCIEX plugin read `.wiff` files natively are
  not redistributable and are not in this repository. `opendial/scripts/fetch-sciex-assemblies.sh`
  fetches them from an installation you already have a licence for. Without them the port reads
  `.wiff` through msconvert instead. Their licence forbids decompilation; nothing here does any.
- **Acquisitions and spectral libraries** — the data the port was validated against is not ours to
  redistribute. Only synthetic data, generated by `opendial/tools/make_synthetic_mzml.py`, is here.
